Anzu is a small, light bird-like man (a tengu) with feathers and a beak, and a member of [[Org/Iconoclasm/index|Iconoclasm]]. He is well-studied in occult and religious matters and is the Party's reader of magic: he identifies what they find, names the creatures they meet, and works out their riddles. He keeps the raven [[People/Othello|Othello]], a pet-shop bird he rewired to carry the memories of the first Othello, killed by fire beneath [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Teller's Run/index|Teller's Run]], and carries a staff of light wood he made himself, with a perch for Othello.

He comes from [[Geography/Austrene/index|Austrene]], where his family, the [[People/Qureshi|Qureshis]], are a noble line that funds [[Org/Belvedere/index|Belvedere]]. He is one of three triplets: his brother [[People/Aguirzu|Aguirzu]] is in good standing, and his sister [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] went missing after months spent with the [[Org/Singers of the Herald's Star|Singers of the Herald's Star]].

Born with his family's psychic gift, he could not reach it until he heard the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]], and the song is the center of his work. He made a sheet of music that hangs a little out of the world, pulled toward the void, and means to strip a song out of a listener, though he needs time to finish the first stage. He speaks in his own mind to a Vocalist he takes for the source of the song.

He has heard the harmony the true kin of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] carry under their sleep, softer than the Voidsong, with the words *ashen pact* beneath it. He believes his sister [[People/Galzu|Galzu]] is caught in the [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]]'s work, and studies the [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] for a way to alter the harmony that holds her without harming her.

He was the only survivor of the attack on the [[Org/Roundhat Gang/index|Roundhat Gang]] at [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Sableclutch/The Crowded Flea|the Crowded Flea]], and killed the half-giant [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Hlarf|Hlarf]] and the gang's leader [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]]. He travels with [[People/Johnny|Johnny Skyfall]], [[People/Benny|Benny]], [[People/Argyle|Argyle]] and [[People/Sir Arctos|Sir Arctos]], and unlike them carries no mark of [[Aut]].
